=== test_r5_ignored_newline_name_is_preserved
ok - an ignored file whose name holds a newline is preserved byte for byte, a changed payload of it refuses, and the one-per-line list refuses that name
exit=0
=== test_r5_history_copy_keeps_a_newline_named_ignored_file
ok - a history-admitted copy keeps a unique ignored file whose name is a newline, as it keeps an ordinary one; clean, it passes
exit=0
=== test_r5_preserve_leaf_moved_into_the_copy_refuses
ok - a preserve whose leaf resolves inside the copy refuses and the original stays; an external preserve passes and survives the removal
exit=0
=== test_r5_stored_bundle_moved_into_the_copy_refuses
ok - a stored bundle whose directory resolves inside the copy refuses at the final proof; an external one passes and restores
exit=0
=== test_r5_failed_preserve_scan_refuses
ok - a failed scan of the staged preserve or of the copy refuses, alone or hiding a changed payload; working scans pass an intact preserve
exit=0
=== test_r5_interrupted_preserve_keeps_the_earlier_one
ok - a failed or interrupted preserve publication keeps every earlier preserve; a successful one is published and verified
exit=0
=== test_r5_landing_admission_rechecks_the_default_ref
ok - a landing admission refuses at the removal when the default ref it read moved or cannot be read, as a retry; unchanged, it passes
exit=0
=== test_r5_stale_bundle_credit_stops_before_the_driver
ok - bundle credit for the driver is rechecked at the final proof: a credited bundle truncated after the credit keeps the copy and the driver never runs; intact, it runs
exit=0
=== test_r5_lock_changed_after_its_first_line_refuses
ok - a lock changed after its first line, or holding more than Vernant's one line, refuses before the driver; unchanged, the driver runs
exit=0
=== test_r5_holder_after_retirement_refuses_before_the_driver
ok - a process found in or holding a file of a locked copy after the retire phase refuses before the driver, named and unsignalled; with none, the driver runs
exit=0
=== test_r5_unreadable_task_record_is_owner_unknown
ok - an unreadable active task record means its owner is unknown and the copy is refused; readable it owns the copy, absent it does not
exit=0
=== test_r5_untracked_managed_hook_file_refuses_like_git
ok - the final proof refuses what a plain git worktree remove refuses: an untracked managed hook file or turn-end marker keeps the copy, an excluded one is removed
exit=0
=== test_r5_landing_cache_reuse_keeps_the_proofs_default_ref
ok - a reused landing proof keeps the default ref it read: moved before the reuse, the final proof refuses as a retry; unchanged, it passes
exit=0
=== test_r5_own_nested_removal_refuses_an_untracked_hook_before_git
ok - the own nested removal refuses an untracked managed hook file at the final proof before Git is asked; clean or excluded, the copy is removed without force
exit=0
=== test_r5_cleanup_clearance_refuses_an_unreadable_task_record
ok - teardown's cleanup-target custody scan refuses when another task's record cannot be read; readable and elsewhere, or absent, it clears
exit=0
=== test_r5_local_only_landing_watches_the_local_branch
ok - a local-only landing with an origin remote present watches the local branch its proof read: unchanged it passes, rewound it refuses
exit=0
